Pages = {71-87},
Month = {JAN 2},
Abstract = {Despite its increasing importance, the phenomenon of party regulation
   has hitherto received relatively little systematic and comparative
   scholarly attention. The contributions to this special issue fill part
   of this lacuna by evaluating the various dimensions of party regulation
   and their impact on the parties and the party systems in
   post-authoritarian Southern Europe. This introduction discusses the main
   sources of party regulation - Constitutions, Party Laws and Party
   Finance Laws - and provides some preliminary conclusions on the
   cartelisation of party organisations and party systems.},
