Abstract = {Research on democratic representation and public opinion formation has
   largely ignored one another. Once one considers the reality of the
   political communication environment, a fundamental tension between these
   two literatures emerges. In this essay, I review work on each,
   highlighting problems with both how ``quality opinion{''} is often
   defined and how representation is typically studied. I then offer a way
   forward.},
